4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,720
The tumor near my brainstem is back.

5
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:10,000
I might forget everything about you again.

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,880
If the surgery works this time...

7
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,760
What if I lose my memories again?

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,520
It's okay.

9
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,480
Just come back.

10
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,160
I don't want to forget.

11
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:23,600
Ever since I was young,

12
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,640
I'd always thought that when I grew up,
I'd have a family

13
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,480
with a father, a mother, and a child
living happily together.

14
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:34,880
I never imagined I'd fall for a woman

15
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,520
until I met Sun.

16
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:02,400
It's pretty.

17
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:06,640
I like it a lot.

18
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,600
I mean the pedestal tray you made.

19
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,720
It's really beautiful.

20
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:14,680
I like it.

21
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,920
If I were the judge,

22
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,720
I'd give you first place.

23
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,320
The first and only woman

24
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,600
I've ever fallen in love with,

25
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,600
who can never be replaced.

26
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:41,600
[Third Person]

27
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:53,120
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

28
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:58,800
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

29
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:02,480
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

30
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:08,840
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

31
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:18,320
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

32
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,760
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

33
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:28,080
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

34
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:37,000
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

35
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:45,520
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

36
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,680
You can start

37
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,320
by telling me what happened.

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
That night...

39
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,080
Nadear didn't mean to
shoot me or anyone else.

40
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,400
We're friends.

41
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,640
The gun just went off.

42
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,320
It was an accident.

43
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:20,120
Is that so?

44
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,200
But the suspect said otherwise.

45
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,200
Ms. Nadear said that

46
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,520
she intentionally shot you.

47
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:40,400
This way.

48
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,680
Thank you.

49
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,400
You know Chris wouldn't hurt you.

50
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,800
Why did you say that?

51
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,000
You know

52
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,520
I won't press charges.

53
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:09,920
You ended up like this because of me and Sun.

54
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,320
No.

55
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,600
Everything turned out this way

56
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,520
because of me.

57
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,600
It's all because of me.

58
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,760
Can you send me your location?

59
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,680
Are you coming to see me?

60
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,000
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

61
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,920
Chris!

62
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,440
Chris!

63
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:46,280
Chris!

64
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,320
Please...

65
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,370
Please help Sun.

66
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:52,400
The accident happened because

67
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,600
I asked you to come see me that day.

68
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,320
If it weren't for me,

69
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:01,600
you wouldn't have lost your memory

70
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:06,600
and would still be living happily with Sun.

71
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,200
It was an accident.

72
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:15,000
You didn't call me to make me crash my car.

73
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,920
That's right.

74
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,080
I didn't want anything bad
to happen to you.

75
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,720
But not Sun.

76
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,840
I was glad that Sun got hurt.

77
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,600
I wanted her to disappear

78
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:36,440
so that it'd be just the two of us.

79
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:44,120
I hated myself for thinking that,

80
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,240
but I couldn't change myself.

81
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,920
I still want her to die.

82
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:01,600
How can we have a fresh start at this point?

83
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,920
The three of us should never have
lived together in the first place.

84
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,600
I'm going to get out of your lives.

85
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,400
But I don't want you to leave.

86
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,800
We're friends, aren't we?

87
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:33,920
And would you want to live with a friend
who wants to kill your girlfriend?

88
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,440
Go and live happily with Sun

89
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,200
after waiting all this time.

90
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,320
Don't visit me again.

91
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:01,000
That's all I ask

92
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,800
of you.

93
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,280
Chris.

94
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:56,000
What's wrong? Can you talk to me about it?

95
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,400
I know you want to protect my feelings,

96
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,200
but I want to protect you too, Chris.

97
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,800
I feel guilty

98
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,240
for putting Nadear in prison.

99
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:24,240
I don't know how to let go of this feeling.

100
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,880
What Nadear said is true.

101
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,920
To move forward,

102
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,320
you have to accept the truth

103
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,480
and move on, too.

104
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:47,600
Nadear wants you to be happy.

105
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:52,000
How can you keep feeling this sad, Chris?

106
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,800
Let's live happily together.

107
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,920
That way, there will be
nothing left between us.

108
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,520
It's not just Nadear.

109
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,480
I want you to be really happy, too.

110
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,520
Mm.

111
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:29,800
Let's be happy together.

112
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,600
I've been living with Sun for several months now.

113
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,920
I'm happier every day

114
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:55,480
having someone I love by my side.

115
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,120
Your cocoa.

116
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:05,920
Thank you.

117
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,600
It's delicious as always.

118
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:16,520
Do your best at work.

119
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,520
Thank you.

120
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,520
I'll take care of that.

121
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,200
You'll have beautifully shaped lips.

122
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,280
Thank you.

123
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:28,360
This is a promotion from our clinic.

124
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,000
Get Botox today

125
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,800
and get a complimentary vitamin treatment.

126
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:34,280
Does the vitamin help brighten the skin?

127
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,000
That's right.

128
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,200
Alright, I'll go with it, then.

129
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,120
- This one, right?
- Yes.

130
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:38,000
One moment, please.

131
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,120
She wants this one.

132
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,640
That's great.

133
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:43,320
Pretty good, huh?

134
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,480
Serve this, please.

135
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,680
Yes, Chef.

136
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,720
Hello, ma'am.

137
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:02,720
I wanted to wish you a Happy New Year.

138
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,720
Sir, hello.

139
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:19,080
[The Medical Council of Thailand]

140
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:22,560
Dr. Jeen had her medical license revoked

141
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,760
after she admitted to an ethics violation.

142
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,720
It's alright, Jeen.

143
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,720
Everyone who wronged me

144
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,120
admitted their wrongdoing,

145
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:54,200
faced the consequences,

146
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,920
and went on with their lives.

147
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,000
I thought I'd moved on.

148
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,040
But in reality,

149
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,800
I might not have yet.

150
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:07,960
Chris, stop.

151
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,200
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

152
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:10,800
Chris!

153
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,280
- Ow!
- Oh...

154
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,320
Sun.

155
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:13,920
Sun...

156
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,800
Don't walk yet.

157
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,000
I'm sorry

158
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,000
for not being careful.

159
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:21,920
Does it hurt a lot?

160
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,320
It's just a small wound.

161
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,120
I don't want you to get hurt,
no matter how small it is.

162
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,120
You know what?

163
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:42,720
I don't want you to get hurt either.

164
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,320
Can I help you work through

165
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,840
whatever is stressing you out?

166
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,640
I'm very happy with my life right now.

167
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,280
I know.

168
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,120
But...

169
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,480
I still can't get Nadear out of my mind.

170
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,320
I can't stop thinking about her.

171
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,680
Then let me try to help you.

172
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,520
Hello,

173
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,880
do you

174
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,920
remember me?

175
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,720
My name is Sun.

176
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,600
I used to go to the same school
as Nadear and Chris.

177
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:57,640
I lived happily, just as you asked me to.

178
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,800
How are you doing, Nadear?

179
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,400
Why are you here?

180
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:07,880
I know... you don't want to see me.

181
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,000
But there's something I still owe you.

182
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,200
Owe?

183
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,000
An apology.

184
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,720
If I'd been strong enough...

185
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:26,440
If I’d handled things better between
my friend and my girlfriend,

186
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,200
things wouldn't have turned out this way.

187
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,320
I'm so sorry, Nadear.

188
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,320
If you apologize again,

189
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,120
I won't let you visit me anymore.

190
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,600
Does that mean...

191
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,200
I can still visit you?

192
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:54,080
I let you visit me today

193
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:56,320
because I'm not angry with you anymore.

194
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,600
Chris,

195
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,920
you should stop blaming yourself already.

196
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,120
You can't help missing this friend, can you?

197
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,240
What's wrong?

198
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,520
I'm happy.

199
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,160
I'm happy to hear you call me "friend."

200
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:21,440
I thought we'd never be friends again.

201
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,800
Maybe it's because you were always kind to me,

202
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:37,120
even after all the terrible things I did,

203
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,120
that I just can't let you go.

204
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:45,400
Thank you for still letting me
be a shareholder of the restaurant.

205
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,440
And thank you for giving Nan's shares
to my parents.

206
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,320
Thank you so much, Chris.

207
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,800
What I've done still isn't enough to
repay you for saving my life.

208
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,440
Then can you do me a favor

209
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,200
so we can call it even?

210
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,800
Chris said you wanted to talk to me.

211
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:07,800
That's right.

212
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,720
I want to talk to you.

213
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,120
I won't let you two
see my daughter ever again!

214
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,000
- Dear, go inside.
- I beg you.

215
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,280
Nadear is like this because of me.

216
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:23,320
I'll do whatever you want to make amends.

217
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,560
Just tell me what you want me to do.

218
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,520
I only ask for one thing.

219
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:30,680
Please let Chris see Nadear one more time.

220
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:34,200
Mom and Dad told me
everything about what you did.

221
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,400
Do you have no shame?

222
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:47,600
You don't have any dignity, huh?

223
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,520
It seems...

224
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:52,880
you love Chris even more than I thought.

225
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,400
Since you're this brave,

226
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:58,400
you won't leave Chris again, will you?

227
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,280
I won't.

228
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,520
I promise.

229
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:12,920
Tell that to Chris.

230
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:17,200
You're not angry at me anymore?

231
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,400
I am.

232
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,800
But I don't want to kill you anymore.

233
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,120
Otherwise, Chris would have no one to be with.

234
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,320
Thanks.

235
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,200
One more thing.

236
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:37,920
I didn't leave the door open
on purpose to let Kiiro escape.

237
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,240
I never wanted Kiiro to die.

238
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:44,720
Then why didn't you tell me?

239
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,120
You wouldn't have believed me anyway.

240
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:56,120
I've always been the villain
in your relationship with Chris.

241
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:00,600
I really did want to steal Chris away from you.

242
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,680
But in the end,

243
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,920
all I got was a fake relationship.

244
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,520
From now on,

245
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,120
please take care of Chris, Sun.

246
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,680
Nadear,

247
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,800
I'm so sorry.

248
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:36,120
I'm sorry for everything.

249
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:38,720
And...

250
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,320
Please know that

251
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,800
you're the best friend Chris ever had.

252
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,200
No one can replace you.

253
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,800
Are you alright?

254
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:03,880
Yeah.

255
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,840
Sun, thank you

256
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:09,000
for talking to Nadear's parents for me.

257
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,480
Do you feel better now?

258
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,200
Mm.

259
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:15,920
That's good.

260
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:19,600
I think Nadear wants you to be happy, too.

261
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,120
Maybe...

262
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:26,600
I might have really gotten
all my memories back now.

263
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:38,360
[Third Person]

264
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:42,360
[Third Person]

265
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,790
[Green Therapy]

266
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:51,700
[Mini Sunflowers]

267
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,360
I didn't think we'd be able to
face each other again.

268
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:05,340
I haven't forgotten, of course.

269
00:20:05,570 --> 00:20:09,060
The person who told me to approach Sun
and helped me regain my memories

270
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:10,470
was you, Doc.

271
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:14,140
It hurts every time...

272
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:15,270
you call me "Doc."

273
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:17,070
Can you call me something else?

274
00:20:19,850 --> 00:20:20,850
Senior Jeen.

275
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:26,580
Being called "Doc" makes me feel guilty,

276
00:20:27,470 --> 00:20:29,170
because I used my profession...

277
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:31,560
to do something so damn terrible.

278
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:34,860
Being called "Senior" is no different.

279
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:38,360
Even though I saw you as
a friend and a junior,

280
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:39,970
I still did that.

281
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,960
Doctors can get sick too, can't they?

282
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,400
You were just mentally ill,

283
00:20:45,470 --> 00:20:46,930
but you're getting treatment now

284
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:48,460
and making amends for what you did.

285
00:20:50,430 --> 00:20:51,260
Yeah.

286
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:52,660
That's the kind of thing

287
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:54,150
I deserve to hear.

288
00:20:57,870 --> 00:20:58,530
So...

289
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:01,670
You're not treating people anymore?

290
00:21:01,890 --> 00:21:03,860
You decided to become a plant doctor instead?

291
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,250
Well...

292
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:13,570
it's probably easier to take care of plants.

293
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,160
I still want to be your patient, though.

294
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:21,160
Can you help me recover all my memories?

295
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,550
I don't want Sun to be
the only one who remembers anymore.

296
00:21:25,870 --> 00:21:26,870
Mm...

297
00:21:28,410 --> 00:21:29,860
I'm not a psychiatrist anymore.

298
00:21:30,170 --> 00:21:31,860
I don't want to call myself that again.

299
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,360
You can advise me

300
00:21:34,850 --> 00:21:36,650
as my senior.

301
00:21:39,670 --> 00:21:40,570
Thank you

302
00:21:40,860 --> 00:21:42,760
for giving me another chance.

303
00:21:44,490 --> 00:21:46,950
But I'll introduce you to a good doctor.

304
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,470
And...

305
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:50,960
as your former psychiatrist,

306
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:52,760
I'm so happy

307
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,960
you're finally getting
your true memories back.

308
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:25,780
What's your name?

309
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:28,970
My name is Chris.

310
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:33,280
I'm an only child.

311
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:52,970
I never thought I'd fall for a woman

312
00:22:56,270 --> 00:22:57,870
until I met...

313
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,160
a woman with a beautiful smile.

314
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:12,160
What is it, Smiley?

315
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:14,840
You don't like it?

316
00:23:18,150 --> 00:23:19,150
Who would like that?

317
00:23:24,390 --> 00:23:25,260
Eat this,

318
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:27,160
so you'll finally stop smiling.

319
00:23:47,470 --> 00:23:50,460
Sun was the first woman
to ever make my heart flutter.

320
00:24:12,110 --> 00:24:13,170
Hey, watch out!

321
00:24:19,870 --> 00:24:20,570
Chris!

322
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,360
What the hell were you doing?

323
00:24:22,380 --> 00:24:23,360
Aren't you afraid of dying?

324
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:25,280
I'm not.

325
00:24:25,870 --> 00:24:27,450
I knew you wouldn't let me die.

326
00:24:27,750 --> 00:24:30,050
Otherwise, you wouldn't be
my soft cushion right now.

327
00:24:32,060 --> 00:24:34,460
Her trust in me

328
00:24:34,660 --> 00:24:37,380
slowly made me fall for her.

329
00:24:43,210 --> 00:24:45,180
Have you read the lecture notes?

330
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:47,470
Did you get to the last page?

331
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:52,070
[032-619-31691, I'm waiting...]

332
00:24:53,420 --> 00:24:56,660
Sun never hid her feelings for me either.

333
00:25:19,070 --> 00:25:21,170
Did you read the last page?

334
00:25:24,450 --> 00:25:25,450
I did.

335
00:25:26,340 --> 00:25:27,770
Why didn't you call me, then?

336
00:25:29,730 --> 00:25:30,860
I just...

337
00:25:31,870 --> 00:25:33,190
Just what?

338
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:45,570
It's fine.

339
00:25:46,770 --> 00:25:47,770
I understand.

340
00:25:54,370 --> 00:25:56,260
But because I was a coward,

341
00:25:56,970 --> 00:25:59,350
my first love came to an end.

342
00:26:00,270 --> 00:26:03,360
After that, there were rumors that
Sun was dating Sa-run.

343
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:07,150
I was heartbroken in silence,
without anyone knowing.

344
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:09,250
Until...

345
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:13,050
we met again

346
00:26:13,250 --> 00:26:15,360
during our freshman year,

347
00:26:15,570 --> 00:26:18,360
when our high school friends
decided to have a reunion.

348
00:26:29,550 --> 00:26:31,760
Are you still dating Sa-run?

349
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:36,080
You mean Aek?

350
00:26:41,360 --> 00:26:42,360
Why do you ask?

351
00:26:51,580 --> 00:26:52,580
Do you like me?

352
00:26:56,660 --> 00:26:58,550
It wouldn't make a difference now, would it?

353
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:00,650
Just answer me first.

354
00:27:03,070 --> 00:27:06,570
If I could go back in time,
I wouldn't make the same mistake again.

355
00:27:11,860 --> 00:27:13,570
The number I gave you...

356
00:27:14,770 --> 00:27:15,960
If it were now,

357
00:27:16,670 --> 00:27:17,770
would you still call it?

358
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,120
How could I?

359
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:22,550
You have a boyfriend now.

360
00:27:35,430 --> 00:27:37,120
I broke up with him a long time ago.

361
00:27:37,650 --> 00:27:38,470
You dummy.

362
00:27:42,670 --> 00:27:44,760
I never really dated him.

363
00:27:46,460 --> 00:27:48,070
I only dated him to spite you.

364
00:27:51,460 --> 00:27:53,160
I never liked Aek.

365
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:57,250
I've liked you all this time.

366
00:27:58,560 --> 00:27:59,560
Then...

367
00:28:01,390 --> 00:28:03,470
Please don't let anyone take my place again.

368
00:28:05,940 --> 00:28:11,520
♫Like the sunlight♫

369
00:28:11,540 --> 00:28:13,800
♫Providing warm embrace♫

370
00:28:13,810 --> 00:28:17,260
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

371
00:28:17,270 --> 00:28:21,270
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

372
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:29,740
♫If you have to face the storm, once the rain goes by♫

373
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,630
♫When you look up high♫

374
00:28:31,650 --> 00:28:34,630
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

375
00:28:34,650 --> 00:28:37,460
We kept our relationship a secret

376
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:39,250
because we weren't ready to tell our parents.

377
00:28:45,850 --> 00:28:49,730
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky,♫

378
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,030
You sure your roommate
isn't coming back tonight?

379
00:28:57,470 --> 00:28:58,280
Why?

380
00:28:58,930 --> 00:29:00,280
What are you going to do to me?

381
00:29:02,710 --> 00:29:05,360
There's something I've always wanted to do.

382
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:08,610
My roommate won't be back until next week,

383
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:12,850
so you can do whatever you want
to your heart's content.

384
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:04,470
I have something to show you.

385
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:10,480
Isn't it pretty?
[CN]

386
00:30:10,860 --> 00:30:12,080
Yes.

387
00:30:13,450 --> 00:30:16,250
But... why isn't it CS?

388
00:30:19,340 --> 00:30:20,640
Where did "N" come from?

389
00:30:21,590 --> 00:30:23,150
Those are our real names.

390
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:25,040
C for Carissa.

391
00:30:25,320 --> 00:30:26,760
N for Natchon.

392
00:30:29,270 --> 00:30:30,670
Using real names

393
00:30:30,690 --> 00:30:32,020
is so lame!

394
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:32,740
Huh?

395
00:30:32,760 --> 00:30:35,360
But we have to use our real names
when we get married, don't we?

396
00:30:37,830 --> 00:30:40,680
Hey, was that a proposal?

397
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:44,080
You think I'll marry you

398
00:30:44,260 --> 00:30:45,870
just because you got this tattoo?

399
00:30:47,950 --> 00:30:49,280
Then will you marry me?

400
00:30:49,920 --> 00:30:50,950
No.

401
00:30:51,910 --> 00:30:53,040
Will you?

402
00:30:53,270 --> 00:30:54,270
No.

403
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,230
You won't, huh?

404
00:30:55,250 --> 00:30:56,510
You won't? Fine!

405
00:30:56,530 --> 00:30:57,650
Will you marry me now? Hm?

406
00:30:57,670 --> 00:30:59,110
No!

407
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:00,640
Hm? Will you?

408
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:01,210
Hm?

409
00:31:01,230 --> 00:31:02,230
No.

410
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:03,910
You won't, huh?

411
00:31:03,930 --> 00:31:04,970
Will you marry me?

412
00:31:04,990 --> 00:31:05,800
Will you?

413
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,640
Will you?

414
00:31:08,670 --> 00:31:09,750
Chris!

415
00:31:09,950 --> 00:31:10,950
Will you marry me?

416
00:31:11,670 --> 00:31:12,580
No.

417
00:31:13,740 --> 00:31:14,830
I won't.

418
00:31:14,960 --> 00:31:16,160
Then take this.

419
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:17,070
Oh.

420
00:31:17,330 --> 00:31:18,690
No way!

421
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,200
Come here.

422
00:31:23,100 --> 00:31:24,560
She has a name.

423
00:31:24,580 --> 00:31:25,650
Call her by her name.

424
00:31:26,490 --> 00:31:27,370
Baby Yellow.

425
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,650
Call her properly.

426
00:31:31,510 --> 00:31:33,170
Her name is Kiiro.

427
00:31:34,830 --> 00:31:36,550
Doesn't that mean yellow too?

428
00:31:37,310 --> 00:31:38,180
Kiiro

429
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:40,350
is so hard to pronounce.

430
00:31:42,770 --> 00:31:43,750
Kiiro.

431
00:31:44,250 --> 00:31:44,660
Ki.

432
00:31:44,670 --> 00:31:45,040
I.

433
00:31:45,050 --> 00:31:45,550
Ro.

434
00:31:46,860 --> 00:31:48,960
Recite that... a hundred times.

435
00:31:49,550 --> 00:31:51,070
Kiiro.

436
00:31:51,370 --> 00:31:52,550
Kiiro.

437
00:31:52,670 --> 00:31:53,840
Kiiro.

438
00:31:54,070 --> 00:31:55,070
Good.

439
00:31:55,260 --> 00:31:56,570
Don't forget it again, okay?

440
00:32:01,290 --> 00:32:03,560
Don't forget about me when you go to Rayong.

441
00:32:05,470 --> 00:32:07,090
How could I?

442
00:32:08,380 --> 00:32:09,380
Then...

443
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:11,170
recite my name too.

444
00:32:12,150 --> 00:32:13,130
Are you nuts?

445
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:16,080
Fine, I'll do it myself, then.

446
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:19,630
Sun, Sun, Sun, Sun, Sun.

447
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:23,550
I definitely won't forget about you.

448
00:32:29,050 --> 00:32:29,680
Come here!

449
00:32:30,130 --> 00:32:31,440
Baby Yellow, Baby Yellow, Baby Yellow.

450
00:32:31,650 --> 00:32:32,460
Hey!

451
00:32:32,610 --> 00:32:34,150
Kiiro, Kiiro.

452
00:32:34,610 --> 00:32:35,670
Baby Yellow.

453
00:32:36,860 --> 00:32:37,860
Kiiro.

454
00:32:38,380 --> 00:32:40,040
Okay, Kiiro it is.

455
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:41,580
Good.

456
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:45,860
Things were going so well between us

457
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:48,050
until...

458
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:50,050
Kiiro passed away.

459
00:32:51,620 --> 00:32:52,360
Chris,

460
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:55,260
are you sure?

461
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:58,960
We don't have to move out.

462
00:32:59,110 --> 00:33:02,160
That day, Sun wanted just the two of us
to move out and live together,

463
00:33:02,260 --> 00:33:04,360
but then Nadear disappeared.

464
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:07,600
We both went out to look for her.

465
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:11,960
Sun.

466
00:33:13,650 --> 00:33:15,750
I wanted to move out and live with you,

467
00:33:16,220 --> 00:33:18,480
not because you were
having problems with Nadear.

468
00:33:19,230 --> 00:33:21,080
I've actually been thinking for a while

469
00:33:22,050 --> 00:33:24,080
that I want to move out and live with you.

470
00:33:26,210 --> 00:33:28,570
I don't mean just temporarily.

471
00:33:31,020 --> 00:33:33,680
I really want to be with you forever.

472
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:48,010
I want to be with you forever, too.

473
00:33:50,350 --> 00:33:52,250
That was the last day

474
00:33:52,870 --> 00:33:54,640
before I lost all my memories.

475
00:33:59,670 --> 00:34:01,260
Now it's time

476
00:34:03,270 --> 00:34:06,110
to make our forever

477
00:34:08,080 --> 00:34:09,440
a reality.

478
00:34:18,570 --> 00:34:22,000
[Third Person]

479
00:34:23,256 --> 00:34:26,026
[Third Person]

480
00:34:32,026 --> 00:34:33,136
Your cocoa.

481
00:34:34,826 --> 00:34:35,726
Thanks.

482
00:34:35,746 --> 00:34:36,426
Mm.

483
00:34:57,406 --> 00:34:58,916
Don't distract me now.

484
00:34:59,296 --> 00:35:00,906
I'm almost done here.

485
00:35:03,136 --> 00:35:04,216
Are you?

486
00:35:05,216 --> 00:35:06,706
Don't distract me.

487
00:35:07,936 --> 00:35:09,326
I'm not.

488
00:35:09,346 --> 00:35:10,716
I just want to take care of you.

489
00:35:18,026 --> 00:35:19,116
What do you want?

490
00:35:23,216 --> 00:35:24,716
Will you indulge me?

491
00:35:27,606 --> 00:35:29,216
Mm...

492
00:35:30,316 --> 00:35:31,826
If it's interesting,

493
00:35:32,726 --> 00:35:34,026
then yes.

494
00:35:41,836 --> 00:35:43,606
Will you leave work behind

495
00:35:43,626 --> 00:35:45,236
to go on a date with me tomorrow?

496
00:35:49,216 --> 00:35:49,826
Mm.

497
00:36:23,976 --> 00:36:24,616
What are you doing?

498
00:36:26,046 --> 00:36:27,926
A mosquito bit me... My leg itches.

499
00:36:33,216 --> 00:36:34,816
It bit through your pants?

500
00:36:35,726 --> 00:36:36,726
Uh...

501
00:36:36,756 --> 00:36:38,026
Maybe it was a wild mosquito.

502
00:36:38,046 --> 00:36:39,496
There are a lot of trees around here.

503
00:36:44,016 --> 00:36:45,296
Here... I'll scratch it for you.

504
00:36:46,716 --> 00:36:47,396
I'm fine.

505
00:36:47,826 --> 00:36:48,926
It's better now.

506
00:36:50,826 --> 00:36:52,706
You're being weird today...

507
00:36:53,026 --> 00:36:54,296
Did you do something wrong?

508
00:36:55,456 --> 00:36:56,416
Nothing.

509
00:36:56,436 --> 00:36:57,526
I'm normal.

510
00:37:02,846 --> 00:37:03,606
Ready?

511
00:37:03,826 --> 00:37:04,776
Ready.

512
00:37:06,116 --> 00:37:06,606
Let's go.

513
00:37:17,926 --> 00:37:19,496
I'm so happy

514
00:37:20,616 --> 00:37:22,216
you let me visit you.

515
00:37:22,816 --> 00:37:25,116
The doctor said I'm doing better,

516
00:37:25,426 --> 00:37:28,116
so I think I can start seeing people again.

517
00:37:29,436 --> 00:37:31,626
I also have something to tell you.

518
00:37:34,806 --> 00:37:36,126
I'm sorry.

519
00:37:36,626 --> 00:37:39,096
Your medical license was revoked
because of me.

520
00:37:41,306 --> 00:37:42,836
Why did you do that, though?

521
00:37:43,126 --> 00:37:45,006
No one pressed any charges against you.

522
00:37:45,216 --> 00:37:46,216
What about you, Nadear?

523
00:37:47,936 --> 00:37:49,216
Why did you admit to what you did?

524
00:37:50,016 --> 00:37:51,336
Chris and Sun

525
00:37:51,616 --> 00:37:53,116
didn't press charges against you, did they?

526
00:37:55,816 --> 00:37:57,706
If I hadn't admitted what I did,

527
00:37:58,996 --> 00:38:00,856
I wouldn't have been punished.

528
00:38:03,246 --> 00:38:04,246
Then...

529
00:38:06,416 --> 00:38:07,796
We admitted to our wrongdoing

530
00:38:07,816 --> 00:38:09,216
for the same reason:

531
00:38:10,716 --> 00:38:12,126
to punish ourselves

532
00:38:13,026 --> 00:38:14,916
so we wouldn't feel
even guiltier than we already did.

533
00:38:17,616 --> 00:38:18,826
Honestly...

534
00:38:19,926 --> 00:38:22,226
you wouldn't have to feel guilty at all

535
00:38:22,246 --> 00:38:23,816
if you hadn't gotten involved with me.

536
00:38:24,136 --> 00:38:25,316
Well...

537
00:38:27,066 --> 00:38:28,326
I already love you.

538
00:38:34,416 --> 00:38:35,736
I'll wait for you, alright?

539
00:38:36,006 --> 00:38:38,916
I destroyed your life.

540
00:38:39,216 --> 00:38:40,726
Don't wait for me.

541
00:38:41,376 --> 00:38:43,486
I don't want to hold you back any longer.

542
00:38:46,026 --> 00:38:48,216
You should find someone better than me.

543
00:38:49,516 --> 00:38:52,726
Think of this as my last request.

544
00:38:55,326 --> 00:38:57,026
If that's what you want...

545
00:39:00,406 --> 00:39:01,806
I'll think about it.

546
00:39:11,276 --> 00:39:12,326
Take a guess

547
00:39:12,716 --> 00:39:14,816
why I brought you here.

548
00:39:16,016 --> 00:39:17,726
Mm...

549
00:39:18,526 --> 00:39:19,616
You wanted seafood?

550
00:39:22,456 --> 00:39:23,516
You wanted to go swimming?

551
00:39:26,126 --> 00:39:28,026
Mm...

552
00:39:28,906 --> 00:39:31,296
You wanted to check out
the girls in bikinis, right?

553
00:39:31,426 --> 00:39:32,676
Whoa...

554
00:39:32,706 --> 00:39:34,016
You're such a perv!

555
00:39:34,366 --> 00:39:35,816
When have I ever done that?

556
00:39:36,226 --> 00:39:37,526
You did when I was wearing one.

557
00:39:38,326 --> 00:39:39,826
You kept staring at me.

558
00:39:40,916 --> 00:39:42,436
I'm only like that with you, alright?

559
00:39:43,526 --> 00:39:44,726
You're a sweet talker, huh?

560
00:39:47,786 --> 00:39:49,416
It tastes bitter to me, though.

561
00:39:49,616 --> 00:39:50,696
Want to have a taste?

562
00:39:52,116 --> 00:39:52,896
Tell me first.

563
00:39:52,916 --> 00:39:54,616
Why did you bring me here?

564
00:40:01,926 --> 00:40:02,926
Don't you remember?

565
00:40:11,116 --> 00:40:12,116
We...

566
00:40:12,336 --> 00:40:14,636
had our first kiss here.

567
00:40:18,036 --> 00:40:19,406
You remember now?

568
00:40:21,356 --> 00:40:22,016
Mm.

569
00:40:22,516 --> 00:40:23,716
I remember everything, too.

570
00:40:24,366 --> 00:40:26,226
I got some help from my psychiatrist.

571
00:40:27,336 --> 00:40:28,656
Are you not afraid of them anymore?

572
00:40:29,916 --> 00:40:31,126
I still am.

573
00:40:32,316 --> 00:40:34,106
But I'm even more afraid of forgetting.

574
00:40:35,536 --> 00:40:38,326
I don't want you to do this alone anymore.

575
00:40:40,016 --> 00:40:41,976
I want to do it for you too.

576
00:40:45,376 --> 00:40:46,526
That's great!

577
00:40:48,006 --> 00:40:49,516
How does it feel?

578
00:40:50,756 --> 00:40:51,916
Mm...

579
00:40:52,446 --> 00:40:53,926
I guess... fulfilled?

580
00:40:54,816 --> 00:40:56,206
The emptiness

581
00:40:56,236 --> 00:40:58,106
and the feeling of being lost

582
00:40:58,126 --> 00:40:59,606
have all disappeared.

583
00:41:00,836 --> 00:41:02,906
And it feels like...

584
00:41:03,176 --> 00:41:05,096
I'm finally myself again.

585
00:41:06,426 --> 00:41:07,236
I'm so glad

586
00:41:08,236 --> 00:41:10,636
you remember our first kiss.

587
00:41:13,016 --> 00:41:14,016
You were so brave

588
00:41:14,106 --> 00:41:15,516
that day.

589
00:41:18,006 --> 00:41:19,326
Me? Brave?

590
00:41:19,816 --> 00:41:21,736
I was a coward for years, though.

591
00:41:23,536 --> 00:41:24,336
By the way...

592
00:41:25,606 --> 00:41:27,806
why did you give me
another chance back then?

593
00:41:30,036 --> 00:41:31,516
Mm...

594
00:41:32,196 --> 00:41:33,196
Honestly,

595
00:41:33,926 --> 00:41:35,666
I was going to give up.

596
00:41:36,736 --> 00:41:37,616
But...

597
00:41:38,106 --> 00:41:39,586
you were so incredible that day.

598
00:41:43,236 --> 00:41:43,956
Why isn't Sun back from
[Seaside Cottage]

599
00:41:43,966 --> 00:41:45,106
surfing yet?

600
00:41:45,116 --> 00:41:46,116
Isn't she taking too long?

601
00:41:46,856 --> 00:41:49,456
Hey, isn't that her surfboard?

602
00:41:50,806 --> 00:41:52,416
Why is only her surfboard floating there?

603
00:41:52,526 --> 00:41:53,626
Where did she go?

604
00:41:54,046 --> 00:41:55,206
Did she drown?

605
00:41:55,566 --> 00:41:57,126
No... She can swim!

606
00:41:57,146 --> 00:41:58,426
But there's only her surfboard.

607
00:41:58,446 --> 00:42:00,016
But she can swim!

608
00:42:00,116 --> 00:42:01,676
Look, she's not there!

609
00:42:01,696 --> 00:42:03,626
She can swim!

610
00:42:03,996 --> 00:42:04,576
Huh?

611
00:42:08,306 --> 00:42:09,206
Sun!

612
00:42:10,216 --> 00:42:10,896
Sun!

613
00:42:13,136 --> 00:42:14,096
Sun!

614
00:42:15,436 --> 00:42:16,916
Sun, where are you?!

615
00:42:21,516 --> 00:42:22,226
Sun!

616
00:42:23,636 --> 00:42:24,636
Sun!

617
00:42:32,226 --> 00:42:33,116
Chris!

618
00:42:33,916 --> 00:42:34,866
Chris!

619
00:42:35,126 --> 00:42:36,466
What are you doing over there?

620
00:42:37,276 --> 00:42:38,516
I'm right here!

621
00:42:53,926 --> 00:42:55,526
They said you'd drowned.

622
00:43:02,616 --> 00:43:03,616
You dummy.

623
00:43:20,816 --> 00:43:23,206
You always say you're a coward,

624
00:43:23,436 --> 00:43:25,456
but you're the best at protecting me.

625
00:43:26,316 --> 00:43:28,706
That's why I can't stop liking you.

626
00:43:32,826 --> 00:43:34,506
Then don't stop liking me, alright?

627
00:43:37,736 --> 00:43:39,026
I don't like you anymore.

628
00:43:44,106 --> 00:43:45,526
I love you now.

629
00:43:47,136 --> 00:43:49,086
You rascal!

630
00:43:49,316 --> 00:43:52,036
You're going to get a good scolding tonight.

631
00:43:54,676 --> 00:43:56,016
I can't wait until tonight.

632
00:43:56,616 --> 00:43:57,946
Can you scold me right now?

633
00:43:58,006 --> 00:43:58,776
Seriously?

634
00:43:59,106 --> 00:43:59,706
Mm.

635
00:43:59,726 --> 00:44:00,496
Alright, then.

636
00:44:00,516 --> 00:44:01,956
You're going to get it.

637
00:44:01,976 --> 00:44:02,586
You've got it coming.

638
00:44:02,606 --> 00:44:03,266
Chris!

639
00:44:03,326 --> 00:44:03,946
You got it.

640
00:44:05,096 --> 00:44:06,606
Didn't you say you didn't want to wait, hm?

641
00:44:06,946 --> 00:44:08,096
Come here.

642
00:44:10,056 --> 00:44:11,306
Are we doing it out here?

643
00:44:11,316 --> 00:44:12,396
Mm... Yeah, right here.

644
00:44:12,406 --> 00:44:13,126
Hey!

645
00:44:13,136 --> 00:44:14,436
You wanted it right now, didn't you?

646
00:44:14,456 --> 00:44:15,336
Hey!

647
00:44:15,346 --> 00:44:16,596
Let me take some photos first.

648
00:44:38,776 --> 00:44:39,536
Where did the ring go?

649
00:44:48,136 --> 00:44:49,496
Can you take a photo of me?

650
00:44:50,026 --> 00:44:51,226
Of course.

651
00:44:57,576 --> 00:44:58,526
Smile.

652
00:45:00,806 --> 00:45:01,606
So pretty.

653
00:45:01,626 --> 00:45:02,306
Let me see.

654
00:45:04,846 --> 00:45:05,616
Hey...

655
00:45:05,826 --> 00:45:06,926
A cotton candy stand.

656
00:45:07,726 --> 00:45:08,726
I'll get some cotton candy first.

657
00:45:08,746 --> 00:45:09,386
Mm.

658
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:11,816
Where did it go?

659
00:45:26,206 --> 00:45:27,316
Where did she go?

660
00:45:47,016 --> 00:45:47,916
Where did it go?

661
00:45:51,516 --> 00:45:54,726
[Third Person]

662
00:45:55,839 --> 00:45:58,759
[Third Person]

663
00:45:59,679 --> 00:46:01,639
Why do I always lose things at the beach?

664
00:46:02,719 --> 00:46:03,279
Chris.

665
00:46:04,999 --> 00:46:05,959
What are you looking for?

666
00:46:08,879 --> 00:46:09,759
It's nothing.

667
00:46:10,919 --> 00:46:12,279
You clearly are.

668
00:46:14,399 --> 00:46:15,159
Uh...

669
00:46:15,199 --> 00:46:16,799
I lost my wallet.

670
00:46:16,879 --> 00:46:18,679
I must have dropped it on the beach.

671
00:46:19,279 --> 00:46:19,999
Wait here.

672
00:46:26,239 --> 00:46:27,359
Where the heck did it go?

673
00:46:31,119 --> 00:46:32,079
Ugh...

674
00:46:42,679 --> 00:46:44,319
Didn't we promise not to lie to each other?

675
00:46:49,679 --> 00:46:51,439
Weren't we supposed to
tell each other everything?

676
00:46:53,159 --> 00:46:55,199
I didn't mean to lie to you.

677
00:46:58,079 --> 00:47:00,479
I was planning to surprise you,

678
00:47:01,359 --> 00:47:03,479
but I lost the ring.

679
00:47:04,879 --> 00:47:05,759
A ring?

680
00:47:06,759 --> 00:47:07,759
Are you...

681
00:47:08,159 --> 00:47:09,639
going to...

682
00:47:09,719 --> 00:47:10,519
Sun.

683
00:47:11,479 --> 00:47:14,039
Can you pretend you don't know yet?

684
00:47:16,239 --> 00:47:17,039
Chris.

685
00:47:17,959 --> 00:47:19,879
It's not the ring that matters.

686
00:47:24,359 --> 00:47:26,159
But what's right here is.

687
00:47:29,599 --> 00:47:31,279
You don't have to give me the ring.

688
00:47:32,079 --> 00:47:33,439
It's okay even without anything.

689
00:47:35,839 --> 00:47:38,359
I can feel your feelings.

690
00:47:40,559 --> 00:47:41,759
Just tell me, okay?

691
00:47:53,799 --> 00:47:54,799
Excuse me,

692
00:47:54,999 --> 00:47:56,559
may I have your ribbon?

693
00:47:57,679 --> 00:47:59,479
Thank you. Thank you so much.

694
00:48:06,199 --> 00:48:07,679
Thank you so much, Sun,

695
00:48:08,639 --> 00:48:10,559
for coming back into my life

696
00:48:10,879 --> 00:48:12,439
and helping me become who I used to be...

697
00:48:16,359 --> 00:48:18,079
the person who loves only you.

698
00:48:19,879 --> 00:48:22,159
I should be thanking your heart even more

699
00:48:24,959 --> 00:48:26,279
for never forgetting me.

700
00:48:37,959 --> 00:48:39,479
Do you remember...

701
00:48:40,759 --> 00:48:43,559
when I said I wanted to be with you forever?

702
00:48:46,519 --> 00:48:48,239
Shall we make it come true?

703
00:49:07,439 --> 00:49:08,879
Will you marry me?

704
00:49:12,119 --> 00:49:12,759
Mm.

705
00:49:13,279 --> 00:49:14,079
I will.

706
00:49:21,839 --> 00:49:27,119
♫That umbrella once belonged to just you and me,♫

707
00:49:27,679 --> 00:49:34,359
♫But there is now someone else under it♫

708
00:50:09,679 --> 00:50:10,279
Hey...

709
00:50:13,439 --> 00:50:14,079
Huh?

710
00:50:15,039 --> 00:50:16,439
How did it get here?

711
00:50:16,879 --> 00:50:18,479
I thought I'd already checked my pocket.

712
00:50:21,679 --> 00:50:22,759
What is it, Chris?

713
00:50:27,559 --> 00:50:28,679
The wedding ring.

714
00:50:31,679 --> 00:50:34,159
Then we don't need this anymore, right?

715
00:50:36,119 --> 00:50:36,879
But...

716
00:50:37,959 --> 00:50:39,239
Let's put this away for now

717
00:50:40,359 --> 00:50:42,879
in case it gets lost during
our thrilling activity.

718
00:50:57,039 --> 00:50:59,159
What exactly is this "thrilling activity"...

719
00:51:00,079 --> 00:51:01,079
you're talking about?

720
00:51:21,399 --> 00:51:23,159
Go ahead and unwrap your wedding gift.

721
00:51:23,759 --> 00:51:24,959
Interested?

722
00:52:33,199 --> 00:52:37,709
[Three years later]

723
00:52:58,399 --> 00:53:00,079
My bride is so beautiful.

724
00:53:00,959 --> 00:53:02,759
My bride is beautiful, too.

725
00:53:05,799 --> 00:53:06,559
Ready?

726
00:53:13,359 --> 00:53:14,799
Of course you two are beautiful.

727
00:53:14,999 --> 00:53:17,599
It took you three years
to pick out your wedding dresses.

728
00:53:18,359 --> 00:53:20,919
Who even takes this long
to plan a wedding anyway?

729
00:53:21,239 --> 00:53:22,719
I actually started thinking...

730
00:53:22,719 --> 00:53:24,559
my friends were never going to get married.

731
00:53:28,039 --> 00:53:29,639
It took so long because

732
00:53:30,599 --> 00:53:33,359
we were waiting for an important guest.

733
00:53:34,399 --> 00:53:35,279
Who?

734
00:53:35,479 --> 00:53:36,479
The Prime Minister?

735
00:53:37,839 --> 00:53:39,359
I can't with you.

736
00:53:40,919 --> 00:53:42,319
Hey, wait...

737
00:53:43,039 --> 00:53:45,359
How did you two meet up?

738
00:53:45,479 --> 00:53:47,039
Don't you know the tradition

739
00:53:47,049 --> 00:53:48,759
that you're not supposed to
see each other before the wedding?

740
00:53:49,399 --> 00:53:50,599
So, choose

741
00:53:50,599 --> 00:53:52,279
which one of you is leaving first.

742
00:53:58,959 --> 00:54:01,119
I think we've decided.

743
00:54:03,159 --> 00:54:03,879
Me?

744
00:54:04,999 --> 00:54:06,359
Go on.

745
00:54:06,359 --> 00:54:07,479
We'll see you at the wedding.

746
00:54:07,679 --> 00:54:08,279
Alright.

747
00:54:08,359 --> 00:54:09,159
Bye.

748
00:54:18,359 --> 00:54:20,119
Let's save our first kiss
in our wedding dresses

749
00:54:20,199 --> 00:54:21,639
for the ceremony, okay?

750
00:54:24,479 --> 00:54:25,599
Okay, Sun.

751
00:54:25,879 --> 00:54:26,879
Understood.

752
00:54:29,559 --> 00:54:30,759
I'll settle for a nose kiss, then.

753
00:54:44,359 --> 00:54:45,359
Jeen.

754
00:54:51,559 --> 00:54:53,079
Isn't your partner coming?

755
00:54:53,679 --> 00:54:55,559
They went on a long hiking trip
with their friends.

756
00:54:56,239 --> 00:54:57,959
They still haven't replied to my texts.

757
00:55:02,559 --> 00:55:05,959
I'm happy you've finally found love.

758
00:55:06,239 --> 00:55:08,639
I have you to thank for
telling me to move on.

759
00:55:14,119 --> 00:55:15,119
Let's get going.

760
00:55:15,399 --> 00:55:17,079
Everyone's been waiting for you.

761
00:55:27,479 --> 00:55:28,479
Let's take a photo.

762
00:55:28,759 --> 00:55:29,559
Alright.

763
00:55:30,759 --> 00:55:32,159
Three... two...

764
00:55:36,079 --> 00:55:37,079
Congratulations, dear.

765
00:55:37,599 --> 00:55:39,039
Take good care of each other
for many years to come, okay?

766
00:55:39,679 --> 00:55:41,159
Thank you so much, Dad.

767
00:55:41,199 --> 00:55:42,079
Thank you.

768
00:55:43,559 --> 00:55:44,519
Excuse me.

769
00:55:44,649 --> 00:55:46,039
Let's head inside

770
00:55:46,039 --> 00:55:46,839
and get ready.

771
00:55:46,959 --> 00:55:47,679
Okay.

772
00:55:50,339 --> 00:55:51,079
Are you tired?

773
00:55:51,359 --> 00:55:52,759
No... Are you?

774
00:55:53,839 --> 00:55:55,189
You two!

775
00:55:55,959 --> 00:55:59,039
Congratulations on your wedding.

776
00:55:59,559 --> 00:56:00,559
And...

777
00:56:00,719 --> 00:56:03,199
don't forget about each other again, alright?

778
00:56:03,479 --> 00:56:04,999
Make sure you never forget each other again.

779
00:56:05,159 --> 00:56:06,199
Okay.

780
00:56:06,559 --> 00:56:07,159
Let's take a photo.

781
00:56:07,199 --> 00:56:08,079
Yeah.

782
00:56:08,839 --> 00:56:09,919
Stand right in the middle.

783
00:56:09,959 --> 00:56:11,199
You're so pretty.

784
00:56:12,749 --> 00:56:13,619
Ready?

785
00:56:13,629 --> 00:56:14,959
Three... two...

786
00:56:15,119 --> 00:56:16,399
One more pose, please.

787
00:56:19,839 --> 00:56:20,839
Okay.

788
00:56:20,879 --> 00:56:21,959
Thanks.

789
00:56:32,959 --> 00:56:34,879
I heard that you two

790
00:56:35,559 --> 00:56:37,919
weren't going to have the wedding without me?

791
00:56:39,079 --> 00:56:40,079
Of course.

792
00:56:41,559 --> 00:56:44,279
You're important to both of us, Nadear.

793
00:56:48,359 --> 00:56:49,199
Let's take a photo.

794
00:56:51,599 --> 00:56:52,239
Come.

795
00:56:52,959 --> 00:56:55,159
You both look so beautiful.

796
00:56:57,159 --> 00:56:58,399
Look at the camera, please.

797
00:56:59,079 --> 00:57:00,259
Three... two...

798
00:57:17,999 --> 00:57:19,229
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

799
00:57:19,239 --> 00:57:23,599
- Kiss, kiss, kiss!
- Kiss, kiss, kiss!

800
00:57:24,199 --> 00:57:25,469
Kiss!

801
00:57:54,079 --> 00:57:55,839
Several years ago, on this very day,

802
00:57:55,839 --> 00:57:58,559
the three of us had a terrible fight.

803
00:58:02,119 --> 00:58:03,679
But today...

804
00:58:03,679 --> 00:58:06,679
time has brought us back together.

805
00:58:07,679 --> 00:58:08,999
We laugh

806
00:58:09,519 --> 00:58:11,279
and are friends once again.

807
00:58:15,479 --> 00:58:17,759
Just as someone once said,

808
00:58:18,679 --> 00:58:21,439
"Time doesn't heal everything,

809
00:58:22,039 --> 00:58:24,159
but accepting the truth

810
00:58:24,399 --> 00:58:25,879
will heal everything."

811
00:58:42,399 --> 00:58:42,959
Alright.

812
00:58:44,279 --> 00:58:45,279
Hi!

813
00:58:45,359 --> 00:58:46,359
Hi!

814
00:58:48,639 --> 00:58:49,639
Let's sit down.

815
00:58:49,679 --> 00:58:51,319
Hi, Yellow.

816
00:58:51,319 --> 00:58:53,959
Mom and Mommy are married now.

817
00:58:59,679 --> 00:59:00,879
But now,

818
00:59:00,959 --> 00:59:03,479
it's time for my bride to take a shower.

819
00:59:06,799 --> 00:59:07,679
No,

820
00:59:07,879 --> 00:59:08,879
I still want to party.

821
00:59:20,719 --> 00:59:21,479
Come.

822
00:59:22,039 --> 00:59:23,319
Aren't you tired yet?

823
00:59:23,359 --> 00:59:24,359
No.

824
00:59:24,359 --> 00:59:25,359
Come on.

825
00:59:41,079 --> 00:59:42,359
For me,

826
00:59:42,759 --> 00:59:45,479
I don't know how true that saying really is.

827
00:59:51,879 --> 00:59:53,479
I only know the past,

828
00:59:53,759 --> 00:59:55,079
the present,

829
00:59:55,359 --> 00:59:57,159
and the future that has yet to come.

830
00:59:58,039 --> 01:00:01,159
And what's most real to me

831
01:00:02,079 --> 01:00:03,959
is the present and
the person right in front of me.

832
01:00:12,439 --> 01:00:20,459
♫If you have to face the storm, once the rain goes by♫

833
01:00:20,469 --> 01:00:22,199
♫When you look up high♫

834
01:00:22,239 --> 01:00:26,079
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

835
01:00:26,079 --> 01:00:29,039
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

836
01:00:29,039 --> 01:00:31,279
My ever-changing present

837
01:00:31,279 --> 01:00:33,439
becomes a beautiful past

838
01:00:34,719 --> 01:00:37,959
and a story that will stay in my memory

839
01:00:38,239 --> 01:00:39,479
forever.

840
01:00:42,199 --> 01:00:46,719
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

841
01:01:05,559 --> 01:01:14,879
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

842
01:01:15,479 --> 01:01:20,599
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

843
01:01:20,639 --> 01:01:24,239
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

844
01:01:24,919 --> 01:01:30,639
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

845
01:01:30,679 --> 01:01:40,119
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

846
01:01:40,519 --> 01:01:45,559
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

847
01:01:45,559 --> 01:01:49,839
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

848
01:01:49,879 --> 01:01:58,799
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

849
01:01:59,239 --> 01:02:07,399
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
